            },
            "reviewBody": "I increased the tequila to 2 oz and it’s really good.",
            "datePublished": "2020-06-06T02:40:56.730Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dave Bartsch"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Your recipe calls for 1 jugger (1.5 fl oz) tequila and 1/2 jugger (1.5 fl oz) grenadine. They cannot both be right. If 1 jigger is 1.5 fl oz, 1/2 jugger is only 0.75 (3/4) fl oz. I only point this out because not everyone has a jigger, and may use a measuring cup.",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-07T04:16:03.261Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very good...but I only used 1/2 cup of store bought orange juice because I wanted a slightly stronger cocktail. The grenadine settled to the bottom more than I wanted, so next time I'll stir it slightly before serving. I can't wait to make this for guests.",
